cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DPP Service — custody-delegation reference implementation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fabianek
    given-names: Christoph
    affiliation: "DID Daten-Intermediär-Dienste FlexCo / OwnYourData"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a custody-delegation architecture for
  standards-based Digital Product Passports: a DPP service provider applies
  lifecycle operations under EN 18222/18223, while a legally separate data
  intermediation service provider stores and publicly delivers the passport.
  Custody is delegated per passport by a statement the data holder signs;
  no shared secret exists anywhere in the flow. A passport can be moved to a
  different custodian without changing any identifier, so the data carrier is
  never reprinted. Includes the delegation profile, a set of signed conformance
  vectors with an independent reference verifier, and the record of a run that
  moved a live passport between two custodians.
keywords:
  - digital product passport
  - data intermediary
  - Data Governance Act
  - decentralized identifiers
  - delegation
  - ESPR
  - unique product identifier
  - data portability
license: Apache-2.0
